WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.418 --> 00:00:04.241
Unit six. Cyberbullying Awareness!

2
00:00:05.191 --> 00:00:09.838
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:12.828
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:17.105
Today we learn about Cyberbullying Awareness. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.796 --> 00:00:23.263
Cyberbullying. Say it with me. Cyberbullying!

6
00:00:26.798 --> 00:00:31.432
Hurtful message. Say it with me. Hurtful message!

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.273
Bystander. Say it with me. Bystander!

8
00:00:42.779 --> 00:00:46.575
Block. Say it with me. Block!

9
00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:53.948
Report. Say it with me. Report!

10
00:00:57.485 --> 00:01:02.719
Screenshot evidence. Say it with me. Screenshot evidence!

11
00:01:06.182 --> 00:01:10.837
Trusted adult. Say it with me. Trusted adult!

12
00:01:14.404 --> 00:01:18.252
Stand up. Say it with me. Stand up!

13
00:01:21.705 --> 00:01:39.589
Cyberbullying happens when someone sends a hurtful message online again and again. As a bystander, I can block and report bad behavior, saving screenshot evidence if needed. Telling a trusted adult helps me stand up safely.

14
00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:43.310
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:44.061 --> 00:01:49.490
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.767
Bystander!

17
00:01:51.975 --> 00:01:57.264
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:57.314 --> 00:01:58.763
Trusted adult!

19
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:07.403
Did you know? Reporting cyberbullying to a platform can help protect not just you, but other people too!

20
00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:09.814
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:19.983
Think and answer. What should you do if you see cyberbullying happening online?

22
00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:21.183
Great answer!

23
00:02:22.213 --> 00:02:27.265
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:27.315 --> 00:02:30.728
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

